  <header class="wrap lesson-hero flow">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href={base + course.href}>ITC 120</a> › Final › Sets and maps</p>
    <p class="kicker">Sets and maps · Lesson 1 of 2</p>
    <h1>Sets in Java</h1>
    <KindChips />
    <p class="lede">A collection with one simple promise: no duplicates.</p>
    <div class="goals">
      <p class="note-label">By the end, you can:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>explain what a set is (an ADT with <b>unique</b>, <b>unordered</b> values) and tell when a problem needs a set instead of a list;</li>
        <li>write A ∪ B, A ∩ B, A − B, B − A, and A △ B for two given sets, draw them on a Venn diagram, and (extra) tell whether one set is a <b>subset</b> of another;</li>
        <li>predict what <code>add</code>, <code>contains</code>, <code>remove</code>, and <code>size</code> return on a Java <code>HashSet</code>;</li>
